    <item>
      <title>Advanced Chemical Handling with Fluoroplastic-Lined Magnetic Drive Pumps</title>
      <link>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-assoma/en/products/lining-pump/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-assoma/en/products/lining-pump/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Engineered Solutions for Corrosive Chemical Transfer 
    &lt;div id=&#34;engineered-solutions-for-corrosive-chemical-transfer&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#engineered-solutions-for-corrosive-chemical-transfer&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lined pumps are designed with external metallic armor and an internal lining of advanced fluorinated engineering plastics. This construction enables the safe and efficient handling of highly aggressive and corrosive chemicals across various industries. The magnetic drive, seal-less design ensures leak-free operation and minimizes maintenance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
